## Summary

**Smart /init — detect existing AI tool instruction files and note them**

### Changes (2 files, +131 lines):

`src/commands_project.rs` (+125 lines):
1. `AI_CONFIG_FILES` constant — maps 4 known AI instruction files to human-readable labels:
   • CLAUDE.md → "Claude Code"
   • AGENTS.md → "Gemini / generic agents"  
   • .cursorrules → "Cursor"
   • .github/copilot-instructions.md → "GitHub Copilot"

2. `detect_ai_config_files(dir)` helper — scans a directory for these files, returns `Vec<(path, label)>` of found ones.

3. `generate_init_content` — now appends an "Other AI Tool Configs" section when any AI instruction files are detected, listing each with its label. Section is cleanly omitted when none are found.

4. `handle_init` — prints a stderr notice during generation: `Found existing AI configs: .cursorrules — yoyo reads these automatically`

5. 9 new tests covering:
   • Detection with no files, single file, multiple files
